' @fileoverview Layout constants for the SearchScreen (peek chip + pull-down overlay).
' Values define screen-space geometry and must stay in sync with the corresponding
' XML attributes / animation keyValues in SearchOverlay.xml, SearchPeekChip.xml, and
' SearchScreen.xml.

namespace searchLayout

  ' Peek chip — pinned search bar. Sits directly above the keyboard at the
  ' same width so the search bar and keyboard form a single visual column.
  ' Top edge at y=54 = 5% top-safe-area edge. x position aligns with keyboard
  ' (KEYBOARD_X = 824) so the bar visually couples to the keys below.
  const PEEK_CHIP_X = 824
  const PEEK_CHIP_Y = 54
  const PEEK_CHIP_HEIGHT = 60
  const PEEK_CHIP_WIDTH = 1000

  ' Two-column layout inside the overlay slideGroup:
  '   Suggestions on the LEFT (left edge x=96 = 5% left safe edge — matches
  '     result row items so the single LEFT-press escape from any left-edge
  '     keyboard key (Q/A/Z/3) reaches it).
  '   Keyboard on the RIGHT (right edge x=1824 = 5% right safe edge).
  ' Both columns frame to the safe area, leaving a 44px gap between.
  const SUGGESTIONS_X = 96
  const SUGGESTIONS_WIDTH = 684
  const KEYBOARD_X = 824

  ' Results row list (SearchRow) translation when collapsed.
  ' Sits below the peek chip (peek chip ends at y=114) with breathing room.
  const RESULTS_Y = 140

  ' Results row list translation when the overlay is expanded. Positioned
  ' just below the overlay's bottom edge (OVERLAY_OPEN_Y + OVERLAY_HEIGHT + 20px
  ' margin) so row 0 remains partially visible as live-typing results populate.
  ' Also prevents the texture-reload flash that happens when content is fully
  ' occluded by an opaque rectangle and then revealed — keeping at least
  ' part of row 0 on-screen means its textures never unload.
  const RESULTS_Y_EXPANDED = 550

  ' Overlay (keyboard + suggestion panel) — slides down from above the viewport.
  ' OPEN_Y: resting position when expanded. y=130 — directly below the peek
  '         chip (peek chip occupies y=54–114 with a 16px gap before the
  '         overlay starts). Peek chip stays visible above the overlay.
  ' CLOSED_Y: placed fully above the viewport.
  ' Height budget:
  '   Keyboard at y=0 inside slideGroup, internal keyGrid height 360 (the
  '     hidden textEditBox reservation is removed by setting textEditBox
  '     height=0 and keyGrid translation=[0,0] in SearchQwertyKeyboard.bs
  '     init — see comments there for rationale).
  '   Suggestion list at y=0 inside slideGroup, internal height = 380:
  '     section label 36 (translation y=0) + list 5×56=280 (translation y=56,
  '     ends at y=336) + 8px gap + pinned Clear button 56 (translation y=344,
  '     ends at y=400).
  '   Suggestion column hits exactly 400 — overlay height matches.
  const OVERLAY_OPEN_Y = 130
  const OVERLAY_CLOSED_Y = -400
  const OVERLAY_HEIGHT = 400
  const OVERLAY_WIDTH = 1920

  ' Slide-in animation timing — matches ExtrasSlider / OptionsSlider feel.
  const SLIDE_DURATION_S = 0.3

  ' Typeahead debounce — a BURST FILTER, and only that. Its one job is to avoid
  ' firing between keystrokes while fingers are still moving; 120ms is below the
  ' threshold where a suggestion list feels laggy and above a fast typist's
  ' inter-key gap.
  '
  ' It is deliberately NOT the mechanism that protects a slow server. That is
  ' SearchScreen.startHintsFetch's single-flight rule, which caps outstanding
  ' hints requests at one and self-limits the rate to one per round trip. Because
  ' the hard bound lives there, this value is not load-bearing — getting it a
  ' little wrong costs a little latency, never a pile-up.
  const DEBOUNCE_S = 0.12

  ' Full-search debounce — 150ms. Coalesces rapid keystrokes so the heavy
  ' multi-endpoint search (Items + Persons + Artists + LiveTv/Programs) doesn't
  ' fire on every keypress. Stale-response guard in onFullSearchResults handles
  ' out-of-order completions.
  '
  ' For context before anyone tunes this: the screen this replaced ran the same
  ' four-endpoint search on EVERY keystroke with no debounce at all
  ' (SearchResults.searchMedias — "if search task is running and user selects
  ' another letter stop the search and load the next letter"), and that shipped.
  ' So this value is already strictly more conservative than production. It was
  ' NOT chosen by measurement, and no adaptive back-off was added on top,
  ' deliberately: the two instrumented orchestrators in this codebase answer
  ' oppositely on work-bound vs network-bound (docs/dev/home-first-paint-
  ' performance.md), so there is no general result to reason from, and ADR 0026
  ' is the precedent for rejecting exactly that kind of unmeasured mechanism.
  ' If live search is ever reported as too heavy on a slow self-hosted server,
  ' instrument this screen the way Home and the grid are instrumented and decide
  ' from the numbers — do not guess a threshold here.
  const FULL_SEARCH_DEBOUNCE_S = 0.15

  ' /Search/Hints limit — keeps suggestion list short enough to scan in one glance.
  const HINTS_LIMIT = 8

  ' Recent-searches cap — MRU window. More than this and the list feels unwieldy.
  const RECENT_MAX = 10

end namespace
